    bio: "Chengyu Li is a digital media narrative artist who focuses on digital spaces, interactive storytelling, and the design of immersive experiences. His work examines how individual memory is shaped, reconstructed, and transmitted within spaces, media, and social systems, and explores—through games, virtual environments, and digital imagery—how technology influences people’s understanding of history, emotions, and reality.\n\nIn recent years, his research has increasingly focused on the relationship between memory, history, and digital media, examining how people understand the past as eyewitnesses gradually pass away, and how technology contributes to the construction and dissemination of collective memory.\n\nThis research direction led to the creation of his graduation project, After End. This immersive artwork combines a first-person exploration game with a digital memorial environment. Using the ruins left after the war as a narrative vehicle, the project guides viewers—through the alternation of pre-war and post-war scenes, environmental storytelling, and interactive exploration—to reinterpret, as they walk, observe, and make choices, how memories of war are constantly reconstructed by society, history, and technology.",
